# One repo, two checkouts: WSL and native Windows.
#
# Git for Windows ships core.autocrlf=true, which wants CRLF in the working
# tree. Pinning LF everywhere keeps the two checkouts byte-identical; nothing
# here needs CRLF (PowerShell reads LF scripts fine).
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binaries git should never touch.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.gz  binary
*.zip binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
